          <attvalue for="35" value="0.8" />
          <attvalue for="36" value="Higher crude prices raise energy-exporting states' fiscal and FX receipts (notably Russia), enabling larger direct procurement and stockpiling of munitions and spare parts and reducing the need to pause purchases, thereby increasing the volume of weapons and material flowing into the conflict." />
